'''tush<sup>1</sup>''' (tush), ''n.'' [< ME. ''tusch'', ''tosch''; an assibilated form of ''tusk''<sup>1</sup>.] A long pointed tooth; a tusk; specifically, one of the four canine teeth of the horse.
{{smaller block|That great wolf [Gardiner], . . . whose teeth are like to the venomous ''toshes'' of the ramping lion.
{{right|''Becon'', Works (Parker Soc.), III. 237.}}
And whom he strikes his crooked ''tushes'' slay.
{{right|''Shak.'', Venus and Adonis, l. 624.}}}}

